cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "certivl: exact rational and certified interval arithmetic"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Vincent
    family-names: Gonzalez
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-3640-014X"
    email: vincegonzalez@me.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/vince-gonzalez/certivl"
abstract: >-
  Exact rational and certified interval arithmetic. Every quantity is a Fraction
  or a closed interval with exact rational endpoints guaranteed to contain the
  true value, and every operation rounds outward, so containment survives
  composition. A computed inequality therefore stands as a proof rather than an
  estimate.

  Validated enclosures for sqrt, sin, cos, tan, sec, asin, atan and pi, integer
  square roots, and certified root bracketing of an integer polynomial by
  bisection with exact sign evaluation. Standard library only; mpmath is an
  optional extra used solely to convert existing mpf inputs.

  This is the kernel underneath four deposited papers on certified computation
  for classical plane-covering problems.
keywords:
  - interval arithmetic
  - certified computation
  - computer-assisted proof
  - exact arithmetic
  - validated numerics
license: MIT
